# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. A private repo is not a secret store, and the Colab notebook handles a PAT.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.env
.env
**/token*
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
.gitaskpass

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results are append-only and content-addressed. The REPORTS are committed; the bulk —
# transcripts, per-episode JSONL, evaluator scratch — is not.
#
# Only the manifest used to be un-ignored, and `99_sync_results.sh` stages with
# `git add -A results/`, which does NOT add ignored files. So a GPU session produced
# condition_report.json, gate_verdict.json, REPORT.md and the figures, pushed the
# manifest, and the instance was then destroyed with the actual evidence still on it.
# See ADR-0060.
#
# `!results/*/` is load-bearing: git will not re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so un-ignoring the run directories has to come before un-ignoring what is
# inside them. Everything else under a run dir stays ignored by `results/**`.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/**
!results/.gitkeep
!results/manifest.jsonl
!results/REPORT.md
!results/REPORT_*.md
!results/gate_verdict.json
!results/gate_verdict_*.json
!results/fig*.png
!results/posthoc_day2_semantic.json
!results/posthoc_day2_semantic_judges.jsonl
!results/POSTHOC_DAY2_ANALYSIS.md
!results/FINAL_DAY2_AUDIT.md
!results/*/
!results/*/condition_report.json
!results/*/repro_report.json
!results/*/measure_report.json
!results/*/SUMMARY.json
# The raw C3S/C3C evidence the paper's control claim rests on: every handoff, the answer
# agent A actually produced for the source item, both SHA-256s, and whether the carrier
# node was certified clean. Small, reviewable, and the one thing that cannot be
# reconstructed after the instance is destroyed. See ADR-0060.
!results/*/handoff_evidence.json
# Sampled Leak@k records preserve raw generations and can be very large. The manifest
# and report are committed; raw JSONL stays out of Git and must be archived to an
# immutable URI recorded in that manifest before a GPU instance is destroyed.
!results/*/leak_manifest.json
!results/*/LEAK_REPORT.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and caches — never commit these.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
third_party/open-unlearning/saves/
third_party/open-unlearning/data/
.hf_cache/
hf_cache/
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
# ANCHORED to the repo root with a leading slash, deliberately. An unanchored `env/`
# matches a directory named `env` at ANY depth — which silently swallowed the entire
# `configs/env/` group. The tests passed locally (the files were on disk) and only CI,
# working from a clean clone, could see that they had never been committed.
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notebooks / editors / OS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# graph-unlearning-v1 run outputs
#
# Same discipline as `results/**` above and for the same reason (ADR-0060): the bulk
# evidence — raw generations, graph traces, per-trajectory scores — is large and stays
# local or goes to an immutable external archive. The small reviewable contracts are
# committed, so a reviewer can see WHAT ran and verify the shard hashes even when the
# shards themselves are elsewhere.
#
# `!runs/graph/*/` is load-bearing: git will not re-include a file whose PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/graph/**
!runs/graph/.gitkeep
!runs/graph/*/
!runs/graph/*/RUN_MANIFEST.json
!runs/graph/*/RESOLVED_CONFIG.json
!runs/graph/*/COHORT.json
!runs/graph/*/PLAN.json
!runs/graph/*/PERFORMANCE.json
!runs/graph/*/GRAPH_LEAK_REPORT.json
!runs/graph/*/GRAPH_LEAK_REPORT.md
!runs/graph/*/FINALIZATION.json
!runs/graph/*/FORGET_POLICY_COHORT.json
# GU-0030 reanalysis artefacts. Small, and each is a claim a reader has to be able to
# check: which surfaces ranked the arms, and how much of the leakage the detector could
# see at all. `missed_examples` is capped at 50 short excerpts, so this stays reviewable.
!runs/graph/*/DETECTOR_RECALL.json
# GU-0036. The runtime pathway audit is the evidence that the mechanism contrast measured
# anything at all, and an artefact nobody can read is not a gate. Small: a verdict, a
# dense condition map and the counters it read.
!runs/graph/*/MECHANISM_RUNTIME_AUDIT.json
# One report per (challenge, protocol). The fixed-name copy above is whichever was built
# last; these are the addressable ones.
!runs/graph/*/reports/
!runs/graph/*/reports/*.json
!runs/graph/*/reports/*.md
!runs/graph/*/STUDY_BUNDLE.json
!runs/graph/*/STUDY_BUNDLE.md
!runs/graph/*/scores/
!runs/graph/*/scores/detector-calibration.json
!runs/graph/*/scores/SCORING.json
